{
  "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
  "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I think because this is largely an international trade case, it's probably useful to put this case in context and to compare it to the facts that gave rise to the passage of Section 271(f) that's at issue in this case. You'll recall that in the Deepsouth case, that was a case involving a shrimp deveiner in which all of the activities took place within the United States, except for the final act that took less than an hour to assemble in a foreign country. In that case, this Court held even that was not within the meaning of the -- of the patent statute as it existed then, and Congress then acted to fill that particular loophole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell us --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Does \"substantial portion\" mean a majority?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: -- four would be enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And so you agree that \"substantial portion\" is an ambiguous term?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I'm not sure if that's true"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: 20 percent? 30 percent? 40? How -- how --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tripp",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the one bright line that we -- that we are drawing here is -- on the face of the statute is that one is never enough. We think that's clear when you look at (f)(1) and (f)(2) together the way this Court read them in Microsoft the first time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we think that's just a critical piece here. This is an anti-circumvention provision. It was enacted to shore up the basic territorial restriction against actually making a patented invention in the United States and then shipping it abroad, and we think it needs to be interpreted with that purpose in mind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So you're not pinning this on the -- on the language here, the substantial portion means almost all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What about the -- what about the text of the -- of the statute? It doesn't say \"a substantial portion of the patented invention.\" It says \"a substantial portion of the components\" of -- of the patented invention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So then the question becomes one of what limits Congress wanted to put in an area where it isn't illegal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Under your test, where there are five, and let's assume that each one is necessary to the operation of the patented device, how do you decide if one is substantial, one out of five?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-14-1538",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7e85f7130c8707a93ecd54a0441dc874d7c13c07a7234c7825cfe81157c6857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7e85f7130c8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in Grokster, this Court, when it was underscoring what \"active inducement\" means, said, quote, \"Showing that the infringement was encouraged overcomes the law's reluctance to find liability when a defendant merely sells a commercial product suitable for some unlawful use.\""
    },
    {
